  "West Highland White Terrier": "The Westie was fixed from the white dogs found among Scotland's old Highland earth-terrier populations. Its reconstructed ancestry combines Cairn, Scottish and Skye Terrier influence. It survives as a modern breed and also contributes to Sealyham and Lucas Terrier lines.",
  "Whippet": "The Whippet was developed as a smaller racing and rabbiting sighthound, fast enough for competition but practical for working-class owners. Its reconstructed ancestry combines Greyhound, black-and-tan terrier and Italian Greyhound influence. It later fed Longdog, terrier and toy-terrier lines while surviving as a popular modern breed.",
  "White English Terrier": "The White English Terrier was a white show-terrier offshoot of English ratting stock, now extinct and important to Bull Terrier and related lines.",
